          "text": "Dear Colleague,\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nThe patient has generalized epilepsy with onset at age 64. Seizures are generalized tonic-clonic and occur approximately once per month. The etiology is immune-mediated and associated with NMDA receptor antibodies. The epilepsy is drug-resistant.\n\nCurrent Antiseizure Medications:\n- Lamotrigine\n- Oxcarbazepine\n- Perampanel\n\nSeizure Burden:\nApproximately one generalized tonic-clonic seizure per month.\n\nAssessment:\nDrug-resistant generalized epilepsy characterized by generalized tonic-clonic seizures, with immune etiology related to NMDA receptor antibodies.\n\nPlan:\n- Continue the current antiseizure medication regimen of lamotrigine, oxcarbazepine, and perampanel.\n- Continue monitoring seizure frequency and burden.\n",
